        "text": "Upside risk comes from renewed layoffs, particularly in manufacturing, or another education-related July composition jump and would land above the interval. Downside risk comes from faster job finding, benefit exhaustion, or delayed claims entry and could land below the interval. A sharp administrative or eligibility change would also place the result outside the interval."
